WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.129
In 2007, Sony released the Nic Cage superhero
flick Ghost Rider, which was both spooky and

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:11.910
cheesy in equal measure, and in 2012, it got
a sequel, Ghost Rider: Spirit of Vengeance.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:16.190
But since the rights to Ghost Rider have reverted
to Marvel, there's been no sign of a third

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:17.850
movie ever happening.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.870
Here's why Marvel won't give Ghost Rider another
movie.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.500
Box office meh

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.770
While the first Ghost Rider film earned a
decent $228 million worldwide, the second

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:34.600
only managed $132 million, which is less than
Tony Stark carries in his wallet for petty

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.280
cash.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.660
"Ya, big man in a suit of armor.

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:40.719
Take that off what are you?"

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:43.530
"Genius, billionaire, playboy, philanthropist."

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:47.809
Considering both films were also lambasted
by movie critics, there's not much reason

00:00:47.809 --> 00:00:51.809
for Marvel to put out another Ghost Rider
film when they have proven properties like

00:00:51.809 --> 00:00:56.679
Captain America and Spider-man to focus on
instead, not to mention new franchises like

00:00:56.679 --> 00:00:59.350
Captain Marvel and Black Panther.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.659
Nic Cage isn't interested

00:01:01.659 --> 00:01:06.520
Even if the stars somehow aligned and Marvel
did decide to tackle a third Ghost Rider film

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:10.659
with Cage, the actor has indicated he's not
really all that keen to climb back on the

00:01:10.659 --> 00:01:12.550
motorcycle, given the chance.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:13.890
As he told Collider,

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.930
"I've said what I have to say.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:17.890
I don't want to say never…anything's possible.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:22.370
But I doubt, highly, that I would be in a
third installment of that."

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:26.939
We're guessing most fans aren't exactly disappointed
with that news.

00:01:26.939 --> 00:01:27.939
Television

00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:31.780
Though he's not on the big screen anymore,
there are still some Ghost Rider stories being

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:36.070
told in live action—they're just happening
on Marvel's Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. series.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:40.109
"You don't get to decide who deserves to die."

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.360
"I'm not the one who decides."

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.579
The newest Ghost Rider, Robbie Reyes, is played
by Gabriel Luna and has quickly become a fan

00:01:49.579 --> 00:01:50.579
favorite.

00:01:50.579 --> 00:01:54.520
Though ratings are down, the introduction
of Ghost Rider has revitalized the show, providing

00:01:54.520 --> 00:02:00.079
a connection to the mystical side of the MCU
opened up by the big-screen hit Doctor Strange.

00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:02.039
Team-up, anyone?

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:03.130
Marvel's great divide

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:07.530
Fans hoping that Robbie Reyes' appearance
in Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. might be planting

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:11.510
the seeds for the newest Ghost Rider to jump
on to the big screen are probably going to

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:12.510
be disappointed.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:15.500
"Claims he made a deal with the devil."

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:16.790
"Which is nonsense."

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:21.800
"Ya know the rationalist in me wants to agree
but, the skull on fire presents a pretty compelling

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:22.800
argument for hail Satan."

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:28.760
So far, the events in the movies have had
only a minor effect on the television series,

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:32.520
while the stuff on the TV shows hasn't even
been mentioned in the movies.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:35.400
"I guess you guys haven't heard about me."

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.540
This is probably because of a long-running
power struggle between movie studio head Kevin

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:44.340
Feige and Marvel president Ike Perlmutter,
who is still in charge of the TV shows.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:48.510
As long as there continues to be backstage
drama between the two, Ghost Rider is probably

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:52.370
stuck where he is: on television, and not
in the movies.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.050
Johnny Blaze is old news

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:58.450
The version of Ghost Rider that Nic Cage played,
Johnny Blaze, seems to just be part of the

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:02.120
current Ghost Rider's backstory in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:06.040
Though Cage himself didn't appear on Agents
of S.H.I.E.L.D., the origin story for Robbie

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.540
Reyes involved Robbie making a deal with the
devil in order to save his brother's life.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:14.720
"And you're right, there was someone there
when I came to.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:21.430
But it wasn't a good samaritan...it was the
devil."

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:25.371
Add in the fact that the show also teased
Quentin Carnival, the carnival that Jonny

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:30.480
Blaze works for, and it seems as though Johnny's
story is just prologue in the MCU.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.560
Of course, Marvel could always do a prequel
series about Johnny's time as Ghost Rider,

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.730
but we sort of already have that in the form
of Sony's two films.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.150
No more crap

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:44.560
The first Ghost Rider movie hit just before
the comic book movie creative renaissance

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:49.130
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe—back when
studios could still get away with releasing

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:51.380
mediocre comic book adaptations.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:56.370
In terms of quality and tone, the Ghost Rider
films have far more in common with last-generation

00:03:56.370 --> 00:04:01.010
superhero movies like Daredevil and Fantastic
Four than they do with modern films like Iron

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:02.840
Man or The Dark Knight.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:07.070
Given the poor reputation the Ghost Rider
films have, it's unlikely Marvel would risk

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:11.960
tainting their perfect record at the box office
with a franchise that carries so much baggage.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.450
Thanks for watching!

